WEBVTT


00:00:14.343 --> 00:00:16.678
Been a while since I was up here
in front of you.


00:00:16.762 --> 00:00:19.848
Maybe I'll do us all a favour
and just stick to the cards.


00:00:22.935 --> 00:00:25.604
There's been speculation that I was
involved in the events that occurred


00:00:25.687 --> 00:00:27.105
on the freeway and the rooftop...


00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:30.234
Sorry, Mr Stark, do you
honestly expect us to believe that


00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:33.904
that was a bodyguard
in a suit that conveniently appeared,


00:00:33.987 --> 00:00:36.698
despite the fact
that you sorely despise bodyguards?


00:00:36.782 --> 00:00:37.908
Yes.


00:00:37.991 --> 00:00:42.663
And this mysterious bodyguard
was somehow equipped


00:00:42.746 --> 00:00:46.166
with an undisclosed
Stark high-tech powered battle...


00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:48.210
I know that it's confusing.


00:00:48.293 --> 00:00:51.839
It is one thing to question the official
story, and another thing entirely


00:00:51.922 --> 00:00:55.133
to make wild accusations,
or insinuate that I'm a superhero.


00:00:58.136 --> 00:01:01.431
I mean, let's face it,
I'm not the heroic type.


00:01:01.515 --> 00:01:03.725
A laundry list of character defects,


00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:06.645
all the mistakes I've made,
largely public.


00:01:06.728 --> 00:01:08.355
The truth is


00:01:13.318 --> 00:01:15.279
I am Iron Man.


00:01:26.081 --> 00:01:27.249
Ivan.


00:01:32.504 --> 00:02:29.978
Vanya.


00:05:09.555 --> 00:05:13.225
270 at 30 knots.
Holding steady at 15,000 feet.


00:05:13.308 --> 00:05:45.090
You are clear for exfiltration
over the drop zone.


00:07:10.968 --> 00:07:15.138
Tony! Tony! Tony! Tony!


00:07:15.681 --> 00:07:17.558
It's good to be back.


00:07:19.601 --> 00:07:21.228
-You missed me?
-Blow something up!


00:07:21.311 --> 00:07:25.482
I missed you, too.
Blow something up? I already did that.


00:07:25.566 --> 00:07:28.819
I'm not saying that the world is enjoying


00:07:28.902 --> 00:07:33.073
its longest period of uninterrupted peace
in years because of me.


00:07:36.034 --> 00:07:41.790
I'm not saying
that from the ashes of captivity,


00:07:42.416 --> 00:07:46.920
never has a greater phoenix metaphor
been personified in human history.


00:07:50.007 --> 00:07:55.929
I'm not saying that Uncle Sam
can kick back on a lawn chair,


00:07:56.013 --> 00:07:57.639
sipping on an iced tea


00:07:57.723 --> 00:08:00.767
because I haven't come across anyone
who's man enough


00:08:00.851 --> 00:08:03.729
to go toe-to-toe with me on my best day.


00:08:08.108 --> 00:08:09.359
I love you, Tony!


00:08:09.443 --> 00:08:11.570
Please, it's not about me.


00:08:12.946 --> 00:08:14.740
It's not about you.


00:08:17.034 --> 00:08:19.995
It's not even about us. It's about legacy.


00:08:20.829 --> 00:08:23.832
It's about what we choose
to leave behind for future generations.


00:08:23.916 --> 00:08:28.045
And that's why for the next year
and for the first time since 1974,


00:08:28.128 --> 00:08:30.547
the best and brightest men and women


00:08:30.631 --> 00:08:32.591
of nations and corporations
the world over


00:08:32.674 --> 00:08:36.178
will pool their resources,
share their collective vision,


00:08:36.261 --> 00:08:39.306
to leave behind a brighter future.


00:08:39.389 --> 00:08:41.141
It's not about us.


00:08:41.892 --> 00:08:45.187
Therefore, what I'm saying,
if I'm saying anything,


00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:47.814
is welcome back to the Stark Expo.


00:08:51.568 --> 00:08:54.238
And now,
making a special guest appearance


00:08:54.321 --> 00:08:56.740
from the great beyond
to tell you what it's all about,


00:08:56.823 --> 00:08:59.326
please welcome my father, Howard.


00:09:01.662 --> 00:09:04.623
Everything is achievable
through technology.


00:09:04.706 --> 00:09:07.000
Better living, robust health,


00:09:07.501 --> 00:09:12.047
and for the first time in human history,
the possibility of world peace.


00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:14.049
So, from all of us here
at Stark lndustries,


00:09:14.132 --> 00:09:18.929
I would like to personally introduce you
to the City of the Future.


00:09:19.012 --> 00:09:22.766
Technology holds infinite possibilities
for mankind,


00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:25.686
and will one day rid society of all its ills.


00:09:25.769 --> 00:09:29.356
Soon, technology will affect the way
you live your life every day.


00:09:29.439 --> 00:09:31.024
No more tedious work,


00:09:31.316 --> 00:09:35.737
leaving more time for leisure activities
and enjoying the sweet life.


00:09:35.821 --> 00:09:38.574
The Stark Expo. Welcome.


00:09:43.745 --> 00:09:46.665
We are coming to you live
from the kickoff of the Stark Expo,


00:09:46.748 --> 00:09:49.626
where Tony Stark
has just walked offstage.


00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:51.295
Don't worry
if you can't make it down here tonight


00:09:51.378 --> 00:09:53.797
because this Expo goes on
all year long.


00:09:53.881 --> 00:09:55.883
And I'm gonna be here
checking out all the attractions


00:09:55.966 --> 00:09:59.511
and the pavilions and the inventions
from all around the world.


00:09:59.595 --> 00:10:02.055
-Make sure you join me...
-All right, it's a zoo out there, watch out.


00:10:02.139 --> 00:10:04.975
-Open up, let's go.
-Hey! Nice to see you.


00:10:05.058 --> 00:10:07.603
-All right. Thank you. I remember you.
-Tony, Tony...


00:10:07.686 --> 00:10:09.229
Hey, hey...


00:10:09.313 --> 00:10:11.773
-Call me.
-Hey, hey, hey, hey. Come on, come on.


00:10:11.857 --> 00:10:14.318
Hello. It would be a pleasure.


00:10:14.401 --> 00:10:15.903
-Okay.
-See you, buddy.


00:10:15.986 --> 00:10:17.070
This is Larry.


00:10:17.154 --> 00:10:19.239
Hey, the oracle of Oracle.
What a pleasure.


00:10:19.323 --> 00:10:20.824
-Nice to see you.
-Call me. Call me.


00:10:20.908 --> 00:10:22.701
-Larry King.
-Larry!


00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:25.537
Yes, my people, my people.


00:10:25.621 --> 00:10:27.164
Come on, Tony. There we go.


00:10:27.247 --> 00:10:29.124
-Very mellow.
-That wasn't so bad.


00:10:29.208 --> 00:10:30.501
No, it was perfect.


00:10:30.584 --> 00:10:32.085
Look what we got here, the new model.


00:10:32.169 --> 00:10:33.879
-Hey, does she come with the car?
-I certainly hope so.


00:10:33.962 --> 00:10:35.047
-Hi.
-Hi.


00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:36.298
-And you are?
-Marshal.


00:10:36.381 --> 00:10:38.300
-Irish. I like it.
-Pleased to meet you, Tony.


00:10:38.383 --> 00:10:40.552
I'm on the wheel. Do you mind?
Where you from?


00:10:40.677 --> 00:10:41.887
-Bedford.
-What are you doing here?


00:10:42.012 --> 00:10:44.723
-Looking for you.
-Yeah? You found me.


00:10:46.183 --> 00:10:49.269
-What are you up to later?
-Serving subpoenas.


00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:52.898
He doesn't like to be handed things.


00:10:53.023 --> 00:10:54.566
-Yeah, I have a peeve.
-I got it.


00:10:54.691 --> 00:10:55.776
You are hereby ordered


00:10:55.901 --> 00:10:58.111
to appear before
the Senate Armed Services Committee


00:10:58.237 --> 00:10:59.863
tomorrow morning at 9:00 a.m.


00:10:59.947 --> 00:11:01.532
-Can I see a badge?
-You wanna see the badge?


00:11:01.615 --> 00:11:03.909
He likes the badge.


00:11:04.034 --> 00:11:06.078
-You still like it?
-Yep.


00:11:08.121 --> 00:11:11.583
-How far are we from D.C.?
-D.C.? 250 miles.


00:11:14.336 --> 00:11:20.217
Mr Stark, could we pick up now
where we left off? Mr Stark. Please.


00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:21.885
-Yes, dear?
-Can I have your attention?


00:11:21.969 --> 00:11:23.053
Absolutely.


00:11:23.136 --> 00:11:26.098
Do you or do you not possess
a specialised weapon?


00:11:26.223 --> 00:11:28.475
-I do not. I do not.
-You do not?


00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:31.061
Well, it depends
on how you define the word "weapon."


00:11:31.144 --> 00:11:33.814
-The Iron Man weapon.
-My device does not fit that description.


00:11:33.939 --> 00:11:35.607
Well... How would you describe it?


00:11:35.732 --> 00:11:38.735
I would describe it by defining it
as what it is, Senator.


00:11:38.819 --> 00:11:42.614
-As?
-It's a high-tech prosthesis.


00:11:42.739 --> 00:11:43.740
That is... That is...


00:11:43.824 --> 00:11:46.118
That's actually the most apt description
Ican make of it.


00:11:46.243 --> 00:11:48.078
It's a weapon. It's a weapon, Mr Stark.


00:11:48.161 --> 00:11:51.248
Please, if your priority was actually
the well-being of the American citizen...


00:11:51.331 --> 00:11:54.209
My priority is to get the Iron Man
weapon turned over to the people


00:11:54.293 --> 00:11:57.671
-of the United States of America.
-Well, you can forget it.


00:11:58.255 --> 00:12:02.009
I am Iron Man. The suit and I are one.


00:12:02.134 --> 00:12:04.553
To turn over the Iron Man suit
would be to turn over myself,


00:12:04.636 --> 00:12:07.639
which is tantamount
to indentured servitude or prostitution,


00:12:07.764 --> 00:12:09.391
depending on what state you're in.


00:12:09.474 --> 00:12:12.436
-You can't have it.
-Look, I'm no expert...


00:12:12.519 --> 00:12:16.315
ln prostitution? Of course not.
You're a senator. Come on.


00:12:17.274 --> 00:12:19.735
I'm no expert in weapons.


00:12:19.818 --> 00:12:21.653
We have somebody here
who is an expert on weapons.


00:12:21.778 --> 00:12:26.491
I'd now like to call Justin Hammer,
our current primary weapons contractor.


00:12:27.492 --> 00:12:30.996
Let the record reflect that I observed
Mr Hammer entering the chamber,


00:12:31.121 --> 00:12:32.414
and I am wondering


00:12:32.498 --> 00:12:36.293
if and when any actual expert
will also be in attendance.


00:12:40.172 --> 00:12:44.510
Absolutely. I'm no expert.
I defer to you, Anthony.


00:12:44.635 --> 00:12:46.595
You're the wonder boy.


00:12:46.678 --> 00:12:48.805
Senator, if I may.


00:12:48.889 --> 00:12:53.352
I may well not be an expert,
but you know who was the expert?


00:12:53.477 --> 00:12:56.063
Your dad. Howard Stark.


00:12:56.188 --> 00:13:00.567
Really a father to us all,
and to the military-industrial age.


00:13:01.193 --> 00:13:05.697
Let's just be clear.
He was no flower child. He was a lion.


00:13:05.822 --> 00:13:08.200
We all know why we're here.
ln the last six months,


00:13:08.325 --> 00:13:12.412
Anthony Stark has created a sword
with untold possibilities.


00:13:12.538 --> 00:13:15.332
And yet he insists it's a shield.


00:13:15.415 --> 00:13:20.045
He asks us to trust him
as we cower behind it.


00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:23.382
I wish I were comforted, Anthony,
I really do.


00:13:23.507 --> 00:13:26.593
I'd love to leave my door unlocked
when I leave the house,


00:13:26.718 --> 00:13:28.136
but this ain't Canada.


00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:29.888
You know, we live in a world
of grave threats,


00:13:30.013 --> 00:13:33.725
threats that Mr Stark
will not always be able to foresee.


00:13:34.852 --> 00:13:36.228
Thank you.


00:13:36.353 --> 00:13:39.064
God bless Iron Man. God bless America.


00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:42.276
That is well said, Mr Hammer.


00:13:42.401 --> 00:13:44.319
The committee would now like to invite


00:13:44.403 --> 00:13:47.531
Lieutenant Colonel James Rhodes
to the chamber.


00:13:47.614 --> 00:13:49.116
Rhodey? What?


00:13:55.455 --> 00:13:58.709
Hey, buddy.
I didn't expect to see you here.


00:13:58.792 --> 00:14:01.420
Look, it's me, I'm here.
Deal with it. Let's move on.


00:14:01.545 --> 00:14:02.588
I just...


00:14:02.713 --> 00:14:04.089
-Drop it.
-All right, I'll drop it.


00:14:04.214 --> 00:14:07.676
I have before me a complete report
on the Iron Man weapon,


00:14:07.759 --> 00:14:10.429
compiled by Colonel Rhodes.
And, Colonel, for the record,


00:14:10.554 --> 00:14:13.640
can you please read page 57,
paragraph four?


00:14:13.765 --> 00:14:16.018
You're requesting
that I read specific selections


00:14:16.101 --> 00:14:17.394
-from my report, Senator?
-Yes, sir.


00:14:17.477 --> 00:14:19.396
It was my understanding
that I was going to be testifying


00:14:19.479 --> 00:14:21.648
in a much more comprehensive
and detailed manner.


00:14:21.773 --> 00:14:23.358
l understand.
A lot of things have changed today.


00:14:23.442 --> 00:14:24.735
-So if you could just read...
-You do understand


00:14:24.818 --> 00:14:27.237
that reading a single paragraph
out of context does not reflect


00:14:27.321 --> 00:14:30.616
-the summary of my final...
-Just read it, Colonel. I do. Thank you.


00:14:31.658 --> 00:14:33.076
Very well.


00:14:34.995 --> 00:14:38.290
"As he does not operate within
any definable branch of government,


00:14:40.292 --> 00:14:44.379
"Iron Man presents a potential threat
to the security of both the nation


00:14:44.463 --> 00:14:45.881
"and to her interests."


00:14:45.964 --> 00:14:47.841
I did, however, go on to summarise


00:14:47.966 --> 00:14:50.636
that the benefits of Iron Man
far outweigh the liabilities.


00:14:50.761 --> 00:14:52.888
-And that it would be in our interest...
-That's enough, Colonel.


00:14:52.971 --> 00:14:54.139
-...to fold Mr Stark...
-That's enough.


00:14:54.264 --> 00:14:55.766
...into the existing
chain of command, Senator.


00:14:55.849 --> 00:14:59.228
I'm not a joiner, but I'll consider
Secretary of Defense, if you ask nice.


00:14:59.311 --> 00:15:01.980
We can amend the hours a little bit.


00:15:02.648 --> 00:15:04.399
I'd like to go on and show, if I may,


00:15:04.483 --> 00:15:06.652
the imagery
that's connected to your report.


00:15:06.777 --> 00:15:09.613
I believe it is somewhat premature
to reveal these images


00:15:09.696 --> 00:15:11.490
-to the general public at this time.
-With all due respect,


00:15:11.615 --> 00:15:12.783
Colonel, I understand.


00:15:12.866 --> 00:15:16.954
And if you could just narrate those
for us, we'd be very grateful.


00:15:17.037 --> 00:15:18.997
Let's have the images.


00:15:20.457 --> 00:15:23.669
Intelligence suggests
that the devices seen in these photos


00:15:23.794 --> 00:15:26.630
are, in fact, attempts
at making manned copies


00:15:26.713 --> 00:15:28.173
of Mr Stark's suit.


00:15:28.298 --> 00:15:33.303
This has been corroborated by our allies
and local intelligence on the ground,


00:15:33.387 --> 00:15:38.517
indicating that these suits are quite
possibly, at this moment, operational.


00:15:38.934 --> 00:15:42.604
Hold on one second, buddy.
Let me see something here.


00:15:43.188 --> 00:15:46.191
Boy, I'm good.
I commandeered your screens.


00:15:46.859 --> 00:15:49.695
I need them.
Time for a little transparency.


00:15:49.945 --> 00:15:51.697
-Now, let's see what's really going on.
-What is he doing?


00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:55.033
If you will direct your attention
to said screens...


00:15:55.117 --> 00:15:56.702
l believe that's North Korea.


00:16:04.918 --> 00:16:07.796
Can you turn that off? Take it off.


00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:09.047
Iran.


00:16:12.551 --> 00:16:16.555
No grave immediate threat here.
Is that Justin Hammer?


00:16:17.222 --> 00:16:19.099
How did Hammer get in the game?


00:16:19.892 --> 00:16:21.810
Justin, you're on TV. Focus up.


00:16:23.979 --> 00:16:26.398
Okay, give me a left twist.
Left's good. Turn to the right.


00:16:28.775 --> 00:16:31.528
Oh, shit. Oh, shit!


00:16:31.612 --> 00:16:32.779
Wow.


00:16:33.739 --> 00:16:37.534
Yeah, I'd say most countries,
five, 10 years away.


00:16:37.618 --> 00:16:38.911
Hammer Industries, 20.


00:16:38.994 --> 00:16:41.622
I'd like to point out
that that test pilot survived.


00:16:41.747 --> 00:16:43.248
l think we're done,
is the point that he's making.


00:16:43.332 --> 00:16:46.543
-I don't think there's any reason...
-The point is, you're welcome, I guess.


00:16:46.627 --> 00:16:49.463
-For what?
-Because I'm your nuclear deterrent.


00:16:49.588 --> 00:16:52.090
It's working.
We're safe. America is secure.


00:16:52.174 --> 00:16:54.092
You want my property?
You can't have it.


00:16:54.176 --> 00:16:55.594
But I did you a big favour.


00:16:56.345 --> 00:16:59.264
I've successfully privatized world peace.


00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:04.645
What more do you want? For now!


00:17:05.687 --> 00:17:08.315
I tried to play ball with these ass-clowns.


00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:11.777
...you, Mr Stark. ...you, buddy.


00:17:12.027 --> 00:17:13.987
We're adjourned.
We're adjourned for today.


00:17:14.112 --> 00:17:16.365
-Okay.
-You've been a delight.


00:17:22.204 --> 00:17:24.456
My bond is with the people.


00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:29.795
And I will serve this great nation
at the pleasure of myself.


00:17:30.128 --> 00:17:31.463
If there's one thing I've proven


00:17:31.547 --> 00:17:34.883
it's that you can count on me
to pleasure myself.


00:18:10.586 --> 00:18:12.087
Wake up. Daddy's home.


00:18:12.171 --> 00:18:13.755
Welcome home, sir.


00:18:13.839 --> 00:18:15.716
Congratulations on
the opening ceremonies.


00:18:15.841 --> 00:18:18.844
They were such a success,
as was your Senate hearing.


00:18:18.927 --> 00:18:20.679
And may I say how refreshing it is


00:18:20.762 --> 00:18:24.516
to finally see you in a video
with your clothing on, sir.


00:18:26.435 --> 00:18:27.561
You!


00:18:28.187 --> 00:18:30.355
I swear to God I'll dismantle you.
I'll soak your motherboard.


00:18:30.439 --> 00:18:33.025
I'll turn you into a wine rack.


00:18:33.567 --> 00:18:35.777
How many ounces a day
of this gobbledegook


00:18:35.861 --> 00:18:36.945
am I supposed to drink?


00:18:37.029 --> 00:18:41.033
We are up to 80 ounces a day
to counteract the symptoms, sir.


00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:43.952
Check palladium levels.


00:18:45.871 --> 00:18:48.207
Blood toxicity, 24%.


00:18:49.708 --> 00:18:52.044
It appears that the continued use
of the Iron Man suit


00:18:52.127 --> 00:18:54.546
is accelerating your condition.


00:18:56.048 --> 00:18:58.425
Another core has been depleted.


00:19:01.887 --> 00:19:03.472
God, they're running out quick.


00:19:03.555 --> 00:19:06.225
I have run simulations
on every known element,


00:19:06.308 --> 00:19:08.352
and none can serve
as a viable replacement


00:19:08.435 --> 00:19:10.437
for the palladium core.


00:19:12.648 --> 00:19:15.734
You are running out of both time
and options.


00:19:19.446 --> 00:19:22.157
Unfortunately, the device
that's keeping you alive


00:19:22.241 --> 00:19:24.076
is also killing you.


00:19:25.577 --> 00:19:26.995
Miss Potts is approaching.


00:19:27.079 --> 00:19:29.998
-I recommend that you inform her...
-Mute.


00:19:33.085 --> 00:19:34.670
Is this a joke?


00:19:36.088 --> 00:19:37.756
-What are you thinking?
-What?


00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:40.133
-What are you thinking?
-Hey, I'm thinking I'm busy.


00:19:40.259 --> 00:19:42.553
And you're angry about something.


00:19:42.636 --> 00:19:44.012
Do you have the sniffles?
I don't wanna get sick.


00:19:44.096 --> 00:19:45.514
-Did you just donate...
-Keep your business.


00:19:45.597 --> 00:19:49.142
...our entire modern art collection
to the...


00:19:49.268 --> 00:19:50.853
-Boy Scouts ofAmerica.
-...Boy Scouts ofAmerica?


00:19:50.936 --> 00:19:52.729
Yes. It is a worthwhile organisation.


00:19:52.813 --> 00:19:56.191
I didn't physically check the crates
but, basically, yes.


00:19:56.275 --> 00:19:58.443
And it's not "our" collection,
it's my collection. No offence.


00:19:58.527 --> 00:20:00.571
No, you know what?
I think I'm actually entitled


00:20:00.654 --> 00:20:02.239
to say "our" collection


00:20:02.322 --> 00:20:05.534
considering the time that I put in,
over 10 years,


00:20:05.617 --> 00:20:07.452
-curating that.
-It was a tax write-off. I needed that.


00:20:07.536 --> 00:20:10.622
You know,
there's only about 8,01 1things


00:20:10.706 --> 00:20:12.666
that I really need to talk to you about.


00:20:12.791 --> 00:20:14.209
Dummy. Hey, stop spacing out.


00:20:14.293 --> 00:20:15.752
The Bridgeport's
already machining that part.


00:20:15.836 --> 00:20:18.213
The Expo is a gigantic waste of time.


00:20:18.297 --> 00:20:20.549
I need you to wear a surgical mask
until you're feeling better.


00:20:20.632 --> 00:20:21.675
-Is that okay?
-That's rude.


00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:23.260
There's nothing more important to me
than the Expo.


00:20:23.343 --> 00:20:24.678
It's my primary point of concern.


00:20:24.803 --> 00:20:27.931
-I don't know why you're...
-The Expo is your ego gone crazy.


00:20:28.015 --> 00:20:29.808
Wow. Look at that.


00:20:31.018 --> 00:20:33.395
That's modern art. That's going up.


00:20:33.478 --> 00:20:36.231
-You've got to be kidding.
-I'm gonna put this up right now.


00:20:36.315 --> 00:20:38.525
-This is vital.
-Stark is in complete disarray.


00:20:38.609 --> 00:20:40.944
-You understand that?
-No. Our stocks have never been higher.


00:20:41.028 --> 00:20:43.363
-Yes, from a managerial standpoint.
-You are... Well, if it's messy,


00:20:43.447 --> 00:20:44.948
-then let's double back.
-Let me give you an example.


00:20:45.032 --> 00:20:46.617
-Let's move on to another subject.
-No, no, no, no.


00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:48.410
You are not taking down
the Barnett Newman


00:20:48.494 --> 00:20:49.995
-and hanging that up!
-I'm not taking it down.


00:20:50.078 --> 00:20:51.330
I'm just replacing it with this.


00:20:51.413 --> 00:20:52.789
-Let's see what I can get going here.
-Okay, fine.


00:20:52.873 --> 00:20:56.001
My point is,
we have already awarded contracts


00:20:56.084 --> 00:20:57.753
-to the wind farm people.
-Yeah. Don't say "wind farm."


00:20:57.836 --> 00:20:59.922
-I'm already feeling gassy.
-And to the plastic plantation tree,


00:21:00.005 --> 00:21:02.132
which was your idea, by the way.
Those people are on payroll...


00:21:02.216 --> 00:21:04.009
-Everything was my idea.
-...and you won't make a decision.


00:21:04.092 --> 00:21:05.802
I don't care
about the liberal agenda any more.


00:21:05.886 --> 00:21:08.263
It's boring. Boring.
I'm giving you a boring alert.


00:21:08.347 --> 00:21:10.641
-You do it.
-I do what?


00:21:10.724 --> 00:21:12.684
Excellent idea. I just figured this out.
You run the company.


00:21:12.768 --> 00:21:15.562
-Yeah, I'm trying to run the company.
-Pepper, I need you to run the company.


00:21:15.646 --> 00:21:17.064
-Well, stop trying to do it and do it.
-You will not


00:21:17.147 --> 00:21:18.815
-give me the information...
-I'm not asking you to try...


00:21:18.899 --> 00:21:20.025
-...in order to...
-I'm asking you


00:21:20.108 --> 00:21:21.318
to physically do it. I need you to do it.


00:21:21.401 --> 00:21:23.153
-I am trying to do it.
-Pepper, you're not listening to me!


00:21:23.237 --> 00:21:25.155
-No, you are not listening to me.
-I'm trying to make you CEO.


00:21:25.239 --> 00:21:27.115
Why won't you let me?


00:21:27.658 --> 00:21:30.661
-Have you been drinking?
-Chlorophyll.


00:21:32.579 --> 00:21:36.834
I hereby irrevocably appoint you
chairman and CEO of Stark Industries,


00:21:36.917 --> 00:21:38.836
effective immediately.


00:21:41.004 --> 00:21:42.923
Yeah, done deal. Okay?


00:21:44.383 --> 00:21:46.969
I've actually given this
a fair amount of thought,


00:21:47.052 --> 00:21:50.973
believe it or not.
Doing a bit of headhunting, so to speak,


00:21:51.223 --> 00:21:54.935
trying to figure out
who a worthy successor would be.


00:21:55.018 --> 00:21:56.812
And then I realised


00:21:59.356 --> 00:22:01.900
it's you. It's always been you.


00:22:03.902 --> 00:22:05.028
I thought there'd be a legal issue,


00:22:05.112 --> 00:22:08.574
but actually I'm capable
of appointing my successor.


00:22:09.283 --> 00:22:11.285
My successor being you.


00:22:13.453 --> 00:22:15.122
Congratulations?


00:22:16.874 --> 00:22:18.458
-Take it, just take it.
-I don't know what to think.


00:22:18.542 --> 00:22:20.335
Don't think. Drink.


00:22:24.631 --> 00:22:27.509
There you go.


00:23:07.257 --> 00:23:10.511
The notary's here! Can you please
come sign the transfer paperwork?


00:23:11.053 --> 00:23:12.804
I'm on happy time.


00:23:19.019 --> 00:23:20.270
-Sorry.
-What the hell was that?


00:23:20.354 --> 00:23:22.773
It's called mixed martial arts.
It's been around for three weeks.


00:23:22.856 --> 00:23:24.942
It's called dirty boxing.
There's nothing new about it.


00:23:25.025 --> 00:23:27.486
All right, put them up. Come on.


00:23:30.155 --> 00:23:35.035
I promise you this is the only time
I will ask you to sign over your company.


00:23:36.245 --> 00:23:38.622
I need you to initial each box.


00:23:39.206 --> 00:23:41.959
Lesson one. Never take your eye off...


00:23:44.253 --> 00:23:45.462
That's it. I'm done.


00:23:45.546 --> 00:23:47.965
-What's your name, lady?
-Rushman. Natalie Rushman.


00:23:48.048 --> 00:23:49.633
Front and centre. Come into the church.


00:23:49.716 --> 00:23:53.512
-No. You're seriously not gonna ask...
-If it pleases the court, which it does.


00:23:53.595 --> 00:23:56.932
-It's no problem.
-I'm sorry. He's very eccentric.


00:24:10.487 --> 00:24:11.655
What?


00:24:15.409 --> 00:24:18.203
-Can you give her a lesson?
-No problem.


00:24:18.495 --> 00:24:20.289
-Pepper.
-What?


00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:23.792
-Who is she?
-She is from legal.


00:24:23.876 --> 00:24:27.963
And she is potentially a very expensive
sexual harassment lawsuit


00:24:28.046 --> 00:24:30.215
-if you keep ogling her like that.
-I need a new assistant, boss.


00:24:30.299 --> 00:24:33.093
Yes, and I've got
three excellent potential candidates.


00:24:33.218 --> 00:24:34.720
They're lined up and ready to meet you.


00:24:34.803 --> 00:24:37.681
I don't have time to meet.
I need someone now. I feel like it's her.


00:24:37.764 --> 00:24:38.849
No, it's not.


00:24:38.932 --> 00:24:40.726
-You ever boxed before?
-I have, yes.


00:24:40.809 --> 00:24:44.771
What, like, the Tae Bo? Booty Boot
Camp? Crunch? Something like that?


00:24:44.855 --> 00:24:48.609
-How do I spell your name, Natalie?
-R-U-S-H-M-A-N.


00:24:48.692 --> 00:24:53.113
-What, are you gonna google her now?
-I thought I was ogling her.


00:24:53.197 --> 00:24:56.867
-Wow. Very, very impressive individual.
-You're so predictable, you know that?


00:24:56.950 --> 00:24:59.119
She's fluent in French, Italian,
Russian, Latin.


00:24:59.203 --> 00:25:01.079
-Who speaks Latin?
-No one speaks Latin.


00:25:01.163 --> 00:25:03.457
-No one speaks Latin?
-It's a dead language.


00:25:03.540 --> 00:25:05.334
You can read Latin
or you can write Latin,


00:25:05.417 --> 00:25:07.002
-but you can't speak Latin...
-Did you model in Tokyo?


00:25:07.085 --> 00:25:08.837
-'Cause she modeled in Tokyo.
-Well...


00:25:08.921 --> 00:25:10.297
I need her.
She's got everything that I need.


00:25:10.380 --> 00:25:14.009
Rule number one,
never take your eye off your opponent.


00:25:15.219 --> 00:25:16.637
Oh, my God!


00:25:18.889 --> 00:25:21.642
-Happy!
-That's what I'm talking about.


00:25:21.725 --> 00:25:23.060
-I just slipped.
-You did?


00:25:23.143 --> 00:25:25.479
-Yeah.
-Looks like a TKO to me.


00:25:27.814 --> 00:25:30.025
Just... I need your impression.


00:25:30.108 --> 00:25:32.819
You have a quiet reserve.
I don't know, you have an old soul.


00:25:32.903 --> 00:25:35.405
-I meant your fingerprint.
-Right.


00:25:38.242 --> 00:25:41.787
-So, how are we doing?
-Great. Just wrapping up. Hey.


00:25:43.038 --> 00:25:46.250
-You're the boss.
-Will that be all, Mr Stark?


00:25:46.333 --> 00:25:48.293
-No.
-Yes, that will be all, Ms Rushman.


00:25:48.377 --> 00:25:50.212
Thank you very much.


00:25:53.215 --> 00:25:54.883
-I want one.
-No.


00:26:28.792 --> 00:26:31.170
You know, it's Europe.
Whatever happens the next 20 minutes,


00:26:31.253 --> 00:26:32.504
-just go with it.
-Go with it? Go with what?


00:26:32.588 --> 00:26:34.131
-Mr Stark?
-Hey.


00:26:34.214 --> 00:26:35.424
Hello. How was your flight?


00:26:35.507 --> 00:26:37.009
It was excellent.
Boy, it's nice to see you.


00:26:37.092 --> 00:26:41.263
We have one photographer
from the ACM, if you don't mind. Okay?


00:26:41.346 --> 00:26:43.432
-When did this happen?
-What? You made me do it.


00:26:43.515 --> 00:26:46.059
-I made you do what?
-You quit. Smile. Look right there.


00:26:46.143 --> 00:26:47.269
Stop acting constipated.


00:26:47.352 --> 00:26:48.812
-Don't flare your nostrils.
-You are so predictable.


00:26:48.896 --> 00:26:49.938
-That's the amazing thing.
-Right this way.


00:26:50.022 --> 00:26:51.732
-You look fantastic.
-Why, thank you very much.


00:26:51.815 --> 00:26:53.650
But that's unprofessional.
What's on the docket?


00:26:53.734 --> 00:26:55.652
You have a 9:30 dinner.


00:26:55.736 --> 00:26:57.487
-Perfect. I'll be there at 11 :00.
-Absolutely.


00:26:57.571 --> 00:26:59.406
-Is this us?
-It can be.


00:26:59.490 --> 00:27:01.158
-Great. Make it us.
-Okay.


00:27:01.241 --> 00:27:03.702
-Mr Musk. How are you?
-Hi, Pepper.


00:27:03.785 --> 00:27:05.662
-Congratulations on the promotion.
-Thank you very much.


00:27:05.746 --> 00:27:07.998
Elon, how's it going?
Those Merlin engines are fantastic.


00:27:08.081 --> 00:27:10.083
Thank you. Yeah, I've got an idea
for an electric jet.


00:27:10.167 --> 00:27:11.251
-You do?
-Yeah.


00:27:11.335 --> 00:27:13.378
Then we'll make it work.


00:27:13.754 --> 00:27:15.214
-You want a massage?
-Oh, God. No,


00:27:15.297 --> 00:27:16.757
-I don't want a massage.
-I'll have Natalie make an...


00:27:16.840 --> 00:27:18.258
-I don't want Natalie to do...
-Don't want you tense.


00:27:18.342 --> 00:27:19.510
By the way, I didn't mean
to spring this on you.


00:27:19.593 --> 00:27:20.719
Thank you very much.


00:27:20.802 --> 00:27:22.763
-Green is not your best colour.
-Oh, please.


00:27:22.846 --> 00:27:24.389
Anthony! Is that you?


00:27:24.473 --> 00:27:25.766
-My least favourite person on Earth.
-Hey, pal.


00:27:25.849 --> 00:27:27.142
-Justin Hammer.
-How you doing?


00:27:27.226 --> 00:27:30.020
You're not the only rich guy here
with a fancy car.


00:27:30.103 --> 00:27:32.523
You know Christine Everhart
from Vanity Fair.


00:27:32.606 --> 00:27:33.732
-You guys know each other?
-Hi.


00:27:33.815 --> 00:27:35.067
-Yes.
-Yes.


00:27:35.150 --> 00:27:36.318
-Yes, roughly.
-We do.


00:27:36.401 --> 00:27:40.447
BTW, big story.
The new CEO of Stark Industries.


00:27:40.531 --> 00:27:41.824
-I know. I know.
-Congratulations.


00:27:41.907 --> 00:27:45.369
My editor will kill me if I don't grab
a quote for our Powerful Women issue.


00:27:45.452 --> 00:27:46.620
-Can I?
-Sure.


00:27:46.703 --> 00:27:49.206
She's actually doing a big spread on me
for Vanity Fair.


00:27:49.289 --> 00:27:51.208
I thought I'd throw her a bone, you know.


00:27:51.291 --> 00:27:52.376
-Right.
-Right?


00:27:52.459 --> 00:27:55.838
Well, she did quite a spread
on Tony last year.


00:27:55.921 --> 00:27:57.256
And she wrote a story as well.


00:27:57.339 --> 00:27:59.383
-It was very impressive.
-That was good.


00:27:59.466 --> 00:28:01.510
-Very well done.
-Thank you.


00:28:01.593 --> 00:28:03.053
-I'm gonna go wash.
-Don't leave me.


00:28:03.136 --> 00:28:04.596
-Hey, buddy. How you doing?
-I'm all right.


00:28:04.680 --> 00:28:05.973
-Looking gorgeous.
-Please, this is tough.


00:28:06.056 --> 00:28:08.684
-Can I ask you... Is this the first time...
-Fromage.


00:28:08.767 --> 00:28:10.269
-Say, "Brie."
-...that you guys have seen each other?


00:28:10.352 --> 00:28:12.604
God, that's so awful.


00:28:12.688 --> 00:28:15.065
Listen, is it the first time you've seen
each other since the Senate?


00:28:15.148 --> 00:28:16.817
Since he got his contract revoked...


00:28:16.900 --> 00:28:19.111
-Actually, it's on hold.
-...when you were attempting to...


00:28:19.194 --> 00:28:21.196
That's not what I heard.
What's the difference between "hold"


00:28:21.280 --> 00:28:23.115
-and "cancelled"? The truth?
-Yes, what is?


00:28:23.198 --> 00:28:25.576
No. The truth is...
Why don't we put that away?


00:28:25.659 --> 00:28:29.663
The truth is, I'm actually hoping
to present something at your Expo.


00:28:29.746 --> 00:28:32.124
Well, if you invent something
that works,


00:28:32.207 --> 00:28:33.625
I'll make sure I get you a slot.


00:28:33.709 --> 00:28:35.919
-Mr Stark, your corner table is ready.
-Yes?


00:28:36.003 --> 00:28:38.213
I actually have a slot this year. Yes, I do.


00:28:38.297 --> 00:28:41.466
-Hammer needs a slot, Christine.
-We kid, yeah.


00:28:42.342 --> 00:28:43.510
We kid. We're kidders.


00:29:05.866 --> 00:29:07.910
Got any other bad ideas?


00:29:12.122 --> 00:29:13.290
Tony!


00:29:17.127 --> 00:29:21.423
Tony and I... Tony... I love Tony Stark.
Tony loves me. We're not competitors.


00:29:21.507 --> 00:29:23.967
Him being out of the picture
created tremendous opportunities


00:29:24.051 --> 00:29:26.553
for Hammer Industries, you know?


00:29:26.637 --> 00:29:29.973
-Everything that Tony and I do...
-Well, what's the use of having...


00:29:30.057 --> 00:29:32.935
-...is a healthy...
-...and owning a race car...


00:29:33.018 --> 00:29:35.979
-...competition.
-...if you don't drive it?


00:29:37.022 --> 00:29:38.565
Is he driving?


00:29:45.823 --> 00:29:47.533
Natalie. Natalie!


00:29:48.450 --> 00:29:49.660
-Yes, Miss Potts?
-Did you know about this?


00:29:49.743 --> 00:29:51.954
This is the first that I have known of it.


00:29:52.621 --> 00:29:53.789
This... This cannot happen.


00:29:53.872 --> 00:29:55.541
Absolutely. I understand.
How can I help you?


00:29:55.624 --> 00:29:56.875
-Where's Happy?
-He's waiting outside.


00:29:56.959 --> 00:29:58.836
-Okay, get him. I need Happy.
-Right away.


00:29:59.586 --> 00:30:01.713
Tony's... You know, he...


00:30:01.797 --> 00:30:03.674
We're not competitive.
You know what I mean?


00:30:03.757 --> 00:30:04.842
Yeah, yeah, yeah. You know,


00:30:04.925 --> 00:30:07.886
-can you excuse me just one second?
-Just read me what you wrote.


00:30:07.970 --> 00:30:09.179
-I will. I will, after.
-Just read it back to me.


00:30:09.263 --> 00:30:10.514
But I have to make one quick phone call.


00:30:10.597 --> 00:30:11.682
-Where are you going?
-This is great.


00:30:11.765 --> 00:30:13.141
-I've got some caviar coming.
-This is great stuff.


00:30:13.225 --> 00:30:14.726
-I'll be right back.
-Look!


00:30:14.810 --> 00:30:16.311
That's Stark.


00:32:14.304 --> 00:32:15.556
Go, go!


00:32:19.142 --> 00:32:20.435
Hang on.


00:33:29.379 --> 00:33:31.215
-Give me the case.
-Here. Take it.


00:33:31.298 --> 00:33:32.883
-Where's the key?
-It's in my pocket.


00:33:32.966 --> 00:33:34.134
Car!


00:34:37.781 --> 00:34:39.199
Oh, my God!


00:34:45.789 --> 00:34:48.333
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.


00:34:49.168 --> 00:34:51.336
-Were you heading for me or him?
-I was trying to scare him.


00:34:51.420 --> 00:34:53.422
-'Cause I can't tell!
-Are you out of your mind?


00:34:53.505 --> 00:34:55.465
-Better security.
-Get in the car right now!


00:34:55.549 --> 00:34:57.301
I was attacked! We need better security.


00:34:57.384 --> 00:34:59.636
-Get in the car!
-You're CEO. Better security measures.


00:34:59.720 --> 00:35:01.471
God, it's embarrassing.


00:35:02.306 --> 00:35:04.558
First vacation in two years.


00:35:09.229 --> 00:35:10.647
Oh, my God!


00:35:11.732 --> 00:35:13.984
-I got him!
-Hit him again. Hit him again.


00:35:14.067 --> 00:35:15.944
Football.


00:35:18.405 --> 00:35:20.449
-I got him!
-Take the case! Take it!


00:35:20.532 --> 00:35:22.201
-Take the case!
-Give him the case!


00:35:22.284 --> 00:35:24.119
Stop banging the car!


00:35:27.247 --> 00:35:28.624
Calm down.


00:35:29.541 --> 00:35:31.543
God! God!


00:35:34.129 --> 00:36:14.795
Give me the case! Please! Come on!


00:37:09.266 --> 00:37:10.934
You... You lose.


00:37:17.274 --> 00:37:19.902
You lose. You lose, Stark.


00:38:13.455 --> 00:38:17.125
Pretty decent tech.
Cycles per second were a little low.


00:38:22.881 --> 00:38:25.801
You could have doubled up
your rotations.


00:38:28.512 --> 00:38:31.265
You focused the repulsor energy
through ionized plasma channels.


00:38:31.348 --> 00:38:34.268
It's effective. Not very efficient.


00:38:35.310 --> 00:38:37.646
But it's a passable knock-off.


00:38:38.564 --> 00:38:39.857
I don't get it. A little fine tuning,


00:38:39.940 --> 00:38:41.733
you could have made a solid paycheck.


00:38:41.817 --> 00:38:45.988
You could have sold it
to North Korea, China, Iran,


00:38:46.071 --> 00:38:48.699
or gone right to the black market.


00:38:48.782 --> 00:38:51.743
You look like you got friends
in low places.


00:38:51.827 --> 00:38:57.374
You come from a family
of thieves and butchers.


00:38:58.750 --> 00:39:01.044
And now, like all guilty men,


00:39:01.962 --> 00:39:04.590
you try to rewrite your own history.


00:39:05.257 --> 00:39:10.262
And you forget all the lives
the Stark family has destroyed.


00:39:11.430 --> 00:39:14.683
Speaking of thieves,
where did you get this design?


00:39:14.766 --> 00:39:17.686
My father. Anton Vanko.


00:39:18.896 --> 00:39:21.064
Well, I never heard of him.


00:39:22.149 --> 00:39:24.860
My father is the reason you're alive.


00:39:25.110 --> 00:39:27.112
The reason I'm alive
is 'cause you had a shot, you took it,


00:39:27.196 --> 00:39:28.739
you missed.


00:39:28.822 --> 00:39:30.032
Did I?


00:39:32.910 --> 00:39:35.037
If you can make God bleed,


00:39:36.038 --> 00:39:38.916
the people will cease to believe in him.


00:39:40.250 --> 00:39:44.588
And there will be blood in the water.
And the sharks will come.


00:39:46.590 --> 00:39:51.011
The truth,
all I have to do is sit here and watch


00:39:51.094 --> 00:39:53.597
as the world will consume you.


00:39:53.680 --> 00:39:55.766
Where will you be watching
the world consume me from?


00:39:55.849 --> 00:39:59.770
That's right. A prison cell.
I'll send you a bar of soap.


00:39:59.853 --> 00:40:02.147
Hey, Tony. Before you go,


00:40:02.231 --> 00:40:05.609
palladium in the chest,
painful way to die.


00:40:23.043 --> 00:40:26.505
It's just unbelievable. It proves
that the genie is out of the bottle


00:40:26.588 --> 00:40:29.049
and this man has no idea
what he's doing.


00:40:29.132 --> 00:40:32.886
He thinks of the Iron Man weapon
as a toy.


00:40:32.970 --> 00:40:37.808
I was at a hearing
where Mr Stark, in fact, was adamant


00:40:37.891 --> 00:40:41.520
that these suits
can't exist anywhere else,


00:40:41.603 --> 00:40:44.147
don't exist anywhere else,
never will exist anywhere else,


00:40:44.231 --> 00:40:45.566
at least for five to 10 years,


00:40:45.649 --> 00:40:50.279
and here we are in Monaco realising,
"These suits exist now."


00:40:50.362 --> 00:40:51.530
Mute.


00:40:53.824 --> 00:40:57.119
He should be giving me a medal.
That's the truth.


00:41:00.664 --> 00:41:04.459
-What is that?
-This is your in-flight meal.


00:41:07.462 --> 00:41:09.631
Did you just make that?


00:41:09.715 --> 00:41:13.135
Yeah. Where do you think I've been
for three hours?


00:41:14.136 --> 00:41:15.304
Tony,


00:41:17.472 --> 00:41:19.725
what are you not telling me?


00:41:23.645 --> 00:41:26.648
I don't want to go home. At all.


00:41:28.901 --> 00:41:31.612
Let's cancel my birthday party and...


00:41:31.695 --> 00:41:34.281
We're in Europe.
Let's go to Venice, Cipriani.


00:41:34.364 --> 00:41:35.574
-Remember?
-Oh, yes.


00:41:35.657 --> 00:41:37.534
It's a great place to


00:41:40.037 --> 00:41:43.165
-be healthy.
-I don't think this is the right time.


00:41:43.248 --> 00:41:45.501
We're in kind of a mess.


00:41:45.584 --> 00:41:47.211
Yeah, but maybe that's why
it's the best time.


00:41:47.294 --> 00:41:49.338
-'Cause then we...
-Well, I think as the CEO,


00:41:49.421 --> 00:41:50.547
I need to show up.


00:41:50.631 --> 00:41:54.927
As CEO, you are entitled to a leave.


00:41:55.010 --> 00:41:56.345
-A leave?
-A company retreat.


00:41:56.428 --> 00:41:58.972
-A retreat? During a time like this?
-Just a ride.


00:41:59.056 --> 00:42:02.643
Well, I'm just saying, to recharge
our batteries and figure it all out.


00:42:02.726 --> 00:42:05.479
Not everybody runs on batteries, Tony.


00:44:17.444 --> 00:44:19.571
Hey, there he is.


00:44:20.280 --> 00:44:21.740
There he is.


00:44:23.659 --> 00:44:26.829
What an absolute pleasure. Welcome.


00:44:27.913 --> 00:44:28.956
Oh, goodness gracious.


00:44:29.081 --> 00:44:32.584
Can we get the handcuffs
off my friend here?


00:44:32.668 --> 00:44:36.171
Forgive me, I'm sorry.
I'm such a huge fan of yours.


00:44:36.255 --> 00:44:40.050
I didn't want to make
a first impression like this.


00:44:40.133 --> 00:44:42.427
He's not an animal. Come on.


00:44:43.303 --> 00:44:45.973
He's a human being. Thank you.


00:44:51.019 --> 00:44:52.437
We're fine.


00:44:54.106 --> 00:44:55.774
My name is Justin Hammer.


00:44:55.858 --> 00:44:59.194
I'd like to do some business with you.
Please sit.


00:45:02.948 --> 00:45:05.409
Dig in. What do we have today, Jack?


00:45:05.492 --> 00:45:08.829
-We have some salmon carpaccio.
-Salmon carpaccio.


00:45:10.289 --> 00:45:12.124
Anything you want here, we got it.


00:45:12.207 --> 00:45:16.295
I like my dessert first.
I had this flown in from San Francisco.


00:45:16.378 --> 00:45:18.255
It's Italian, though.


00:45:18.338 --> 00:45:20.132
Organic ice cream.


00:45:20.215 --> 00:45:24.136
I got a sweet tooth.
Apparently you do, too, for Tony Stark.


00:45:26.054 --> 00:45:28.849
What I saw you do to Tony Stark
on that track,


00:45:28.974 --> 00:45:32.603
how you stepped up to him
in front of God and everybody,


00:45:32.686 --> 00:45:34.813
that was... Wow!


00:45:34.897 --> 00:45:36.440
You spoke to me with what you did.


00:45:36.523 --> 00:45:39.151
And I know that you knew
that I'd be listening.


00:45:39.234 --> 00:45:40.777
This is why I couldn't bear
to have you shipped off


00:45:40.861 --> 00:45:43.655
to God knows where. It would have been
such a waste of talent.


00:45:43.739 --> 00:45:45.073
But if I might make a suggestion,


00:45:45.157 --> 00:45:47.868
you know,
you don't just go and try and kill the guy.


00:45:47.993 --> 00:45:52.206
I think, if I may, you go after his legacy.


00:45:52.331 --> 00:45:54.374
That's what you kill.


00:45:54.500 --> 00:45:57.461
You and me,
we are a lot alike in a lot of ways.


00:45:57.544 --> 00:46:02.174
The only difference between you and I
is that I have resources.


00:46:03.008 --> 00:46:05.427
I think, if I may,


00:46:05.511 --> 00:46:07.846
you need my resources.


00:46:07.930 --> 00:46:10.516
Someone behind you, a benefactor.


00:46:10.599 --> 00:46:12.684
I'd like to be that guy.


00:46:24.571 --> 00:46:28.867
Okay. Do you speak English?
Because I can get a translator.


00:46:28.951 --> 00:46:31.787
I don't know. Have you been
understanding everything I'm saying?


00:46:31.870 --> 00:46:33.288
Very good, man.


00:46:33.372 --> 00:46:36.542
-Very good, man.
-Very good, man.


00:46:36.625 --> 00:46:37.751
Hey!


00:46:39.294 --> 00:46:41.463
-Hey.
-Yes?


00:46:41.547 --> 00:46:43.131
I want my bird.


00:46:45.133 --> 00:46:48.804
-A bird? You want a bird?
-I want my bird.


00:46:48.887 --> 00:46:50.556
I can get you a bird.
I can get you 10 birds.


00:46:50.639 --> 00:46:52.182
I want my bird.


00:46:52.266 --> 00:46:54.810
Well, okay.
Nothing's impossible. I could...


00:46:54.893 --> 00:46:58.564
Are we talking about...
Is this a bird back in Russia?


00:46:58.647 --> 00:47:01.692
Yes, but the fundamentals
of the company are still very, very strong


00:47:01.775 --> 00:47:03.694
-despite the events in Monaco.
-Yes, of course.


00:47:03.777 --> 00:47:07.239
-The AP wants a quote.
-Don't tell him. Fax them...


00:47:07.322 --> 00:47:08.824
Where is he?


00:47:08.907 --> 00:47:10.701
-He doesn't want to be disturbed.
-He's downstairs.


00:47:10.784 --> 00:47:12.244
-...what happened in Monaco?
-Yes, but...


00:47:12.327 --> 00:47:14.830
But his continuing erratic behaviour


00:47:14.913 --> 00:47:17.040
may lead many people
to ask themselves,


00:47:17.124 --> 00:47:18.959
"Can this man still protect us?"


00:47:19.084 --> 00:47:22.337
Iron Man never stopped protecting us.
The events in Monaco proved that.


00:47:23.630 --> 00:47:28.010
Query complete, sir.
Anton Vanko was a Soviet physicist


00:47:28.093 --> 00:47:31.096
who defected to the United States
in 1963.


00:47:31.180 --> 00:47:35.350
However, he was accused of espionage
and was deported in 1967.


00:47:35.434 --> 00:47:37.811
His son, Ivan, who is also a physicist,


00:47:37.936 --> 00:47:42.649
was convicted of selling Soviet-era
weapons-grade plutonium to Pakistan,


00:47:42.774 --> 00:47:45.235
and served 15 years in Kopeisk prison.


00:47:45.319 --> 00:47:47.446
No further records exist.


00:47:51.992 --> 00:47:53.619
Tony, you gotta get upstairs


00:47:53.702 --> 00:47:55.954
and get on top
of this situation right now.


00:47:56.038 --> 00:47:59.041
Listen. I've been on the phone
with the National Guard all day,


00:48:00.375 --> 00:48:03.212
trying to talk them out
of rolling tanks up the PCH,


00:48:03.295 --> 00:48:06.173
knocking down your front door
and taking these.


00:48:06.298 --> 00:48:08.300
They're gonna take your suits,
Tony, okay?


00:48:08.383 --> 00:48:10.302
They're sick of the games.


00:48:10.385 --> 00:48:13.597
You said nobody else would possess
this technology for 20 years.


00:48:13.680 --> 00:48:16.892
Well, guess what?
Somebody else had it yesterday.


00:48:16.975 --> 00:48:19.311
It's not theoretical any more.


00:48:20.521 --> 00:48:22.564
Are you listening to me?


00:48:24.691 --> 00:48:26.318
-Are you okay?
-Let's go.


00:48:30.697 --> 00:48:33.242
Hey, man. Hey, hey!


00:48:35.577 --> 00:48:38.956
-You all right?
-Yeah, I should get to my desk.


00:48:39.039 --> 00:48:41.166
-See that cigar box?
-Yeah.


00:48:41.542 --> 00:48:43.168
It's palladium.


00:48:50.175 --> 00:48:51.635
Is that supposed to be smoking?


00:48:51.718 --> 00:48:56.014
If you must know, it's neutron damage.
It's from the reactor wall.


00:48:59.726 --> 00:49:01.854
You had this in your body?


00:49:06.692 --> 00:49:10.529
And how about the high-tech
crossword puzzle on your neck?


00:49:10.612 --> 00:49:12.030
Road rash.


00:49:15.409 --> 00:49:16.785
Thank you.


00:49:28.213 --> 00:49:31.717
-What are you looking at?
-I'm looking at you.


00:49:31.800 --> 00:49:34.845
You wanna do
this whole lone gunslinger act


00:49:34.928 --> 00:49:36.972
and it's unnecessary.
You don't have to do this alone.


00:49:37.055 --> 00:49:39.266
You know, I wish I could believe that.
I really do.


00:49:39.391 --> 00:49:41.602
But you've gotta trust me.


00:49:41.727 --> 00:49:45.481
Contrary to popular belief,
I know exactly what I'm doing.


00:49:54.239 --> 00:49:56.533
This is where we do it.
This is my humble abode.


00:49:56.617 --> 00:50:00.078
You can work in absolute peace.
Must be fun to be dead, right?


00:50:00.162 --> 00:50:01.580
No pressure.


00:50:01.663 --> 00:50:04.666
Here they are. I'm very excited.
They're combat-ready.


00:50:04.750 --> 00:50:06.210
I may have done a few miscalculations


00:50:06.293 --> 00:50:08.295
and rushed the prototype
into production.


00:50:08.420 --> 00:50:10.255
Sue me, I'm enthusiastic.


00:50:10.339 --> 00:50:12.633
Go ahead, take a look around.


00:50:17.429 --> 00:50:19.348
You don't wanna do that.


00:50:19.431 --> 00:50:21.058
You'll be able to access that


00:50:21.141 --> 00:50:23.060
as soon as we generate
some encrypted pass codes.


00:50:23.143 --> 00:50:25.229
Can we generate
some encrypted pass codes?


00:50:25.312 --> 00:50:28.440
Get some of those
encrypted pass codes, Jack.


00:50:29.608 --> 00:50:31.276
Never mind, I...


00:50:32.528 --> 00:50:35.823
Wow. Okay. Good stuff.


00:50:38.283 --> 00:50:40.619
-Sorry?
-Software shit.


00:50:42.871 --> 00:50:44.122
Well...


00:50:45.624 --> 00:50:47.042
You're good.


00:50:47.292 --> 00:50:50.462
You really blasted in
past the firewall there.


00:50:51.713 --> 00:50:54.591
Let me show you where
you're gonna be working primarily.


00:50:54.675 --> 00:50:56.635
Go ahead, take a look.


00:50:57.511 --> 00:51:00.138
Get a good look at that.
That's something, isn't it?


00:51:00.222 --> 00:51:02.224
You know,
those are really just for show and tell.


00:51:02.307 --> 00:51:07.312
They're $1 25.7 million a pop, so...
Wait! Oh, gosh.


00:51:09.398 --> 00:51:12.317
Jesus Christ. Get somebody up here.


00:51:13.152 --> 00:51:15.737
That's where the pilot goes.


00:51:15.821 --> 00:51:19.867
I'm having a tough time
finding volunteers.


00:51:19.992 --> 00:51:23.120
I'll take care of that, just leave it.


00:51:23.203 --> 00:51:24.705
What you want them do?


00:51:24.830 --> 00:51:30.002
Well, long term, I want them to put me
in the Pentagon for the next 25 years.


00:51:30.085 --> 00:51:32.129
I want to make Iron Man
look like an antique.


00:51:32.212 --> 00:51:33.338
I wanna go to that Stark Expo,


00:51:33.422 --> 00:51:35.340
I wanna take a dump
in Tony's front yard.


00:51:35.424 --> 00:51:36.842
You know what I'm talking about?


00:51:36.925 --> 00:51:39.094
-I can do that. No problem.
-Yeah?


00:51:39.178 --> 00:51:41.346
Hey, fabulous! I love it.


00:51:41.430 --> 00:51:44.141
Hey, this is our guy. Didn't I tell you?
I had a feeling.


00:51:53.734 --> 00:51:56.195
Do you know which watch
you'd like to wear tonight, Mr Stark?


00:51:56.528 --> 00:51:58.530
I'll give them a look.


00:52:01.408 --> 00:52:02.868
I should cancel the party.


00:52:03.952 --> 00:52:05.204
-Probably.
-Yeah.


00:52:05.287 --> 00:52:07.915
-'Cause it's...
-Ill-timed.


00:52:08.040 --> 00:52:09.500
Right, sends the wrong message.


00:52:09.583 --> 00:52:11.084
Inappropriate.


00:52:16.924 --> 00:52:19.218
Is that dirty enough for you?


00:52:20.219 --> 00:52:23.972
Gold face, brown band.
The Jaeger. I'll give that a look.


00:52:24.473 --> 00:52:25.933
Bring them over here.


00:52:29.228 --> 00:52:31.396
I'll take that. Why don't you...


00:52:43.450 --> 00:52:45.786
I gotta say it.
It's hard to get a read on you.


00:52:46.078 --> 00:52:48.247
-Where are you from?
-Legal.


00:52:50.958 --> 00:52:53.085
Can I ask you a question,
hypothetically?


00:52:53.168 --> 00:52:54.461
Bit odd.


00:52:54.753 --> 00:52:58.131
If this was your last birthday party
you were ever gonna have,


00:52:58.257 --> 00:52:59.800
how would you celebrate it?


00:53:02.469 --> 00:53:06.640
I'd do whatever I wanted to do
with whoever I wanted to do it with.


00:53:37.296 --> 00:53:39.464
-Good evening.
-Good evening.


00:53:40.382 --> 00:53:42.342
Yes, sir, I understand.


00:53:42.968 --> 00:53:46.680
No. No, sir, that will not be necessary.
I'll handle it.


00:53:46.805 --> 00:53:49.099
Sir, I personally guarantee
that within 24 hours,


00:53:49.183 --> 00:53:51.018
Iron Man will be back on watch.


00:53:58.317 --> 00:53:59.818
Hey, Pepper.


00:54:00.152 --> 00:54:02.237
I'm going to go get some air.


00:54:02.321 --> 00:54:03.697
What's wrong?


00:54:04.490 --> 00:54:06.825
-I don't know what to do.
-You gotta be kidding me.


00:54:12.998 --> 00:54:15.626
-That's it. I'm making... Pepper.
-No, no, no. Don't call anyone.


00:54:15.709 --> 00:54:17.628
This is ridiculous.
I just stuck my neck out for this guy.


00:54:17.711 --> 00:54:18.962
I know. I know. I get it.


00:54:19.046 --> 00:54:20.297
I'm gonna handle it, okay?
Just let me handle it.


00:54:20.380 --> 00:54:23.342
Handle it. Or I'm gonna have to.


00:54:24.510 --> 00:54:26.178
You know, the question
I get asked most often is,


00:54:26.261 --> 00:54:28.764
"Tony, how do you go to the bathroom
in the suit?"


00:54:32.184 --> 00:54:33.602
Just like that.


00:54:37.231 --> 00:54:40.192
Does this guy know
how to throw a party or what?


00:54:43.862 --> 00:54:44.905
I love you.


00:54:45.030 --> 00:54:47.658
Unbelievable! Thank you so much.


00:54:47.741 --> 00:54:51.703
Tony, we all thank you so much
for such a wonderful night.


00:54:51.787 --> 00:54:55.791
And we're gonna say good night now,
and thank you all for coming.


00:54:55.874 --> 00:54:57.084
No, no, no, we can't... Wait, wait, wait.


00:54:57.209 --> 00:54:58.961
We didn't have the cake.
We didn't blow out the candles.


00:54:59.044 --> 00:55:01.839
You're out of control, okay?
Trust me on this one, okay?


00:55:01.922 --> 00:55:04.258
-You're out of control, gorgeous.
-It's time to go to bed. It's time.


00:55:04.383 --> 00:55:05.467
-Give me another smooch.
-You're not going to be


00:55:05.551 --> 00:55:06.760
-happy about this.
-Come on, you know you want to.


00:55:06.885 --> 00:55:08.220
You just peed the suit.


00:55:08.303 --> 00:55:09.763
-I know. It has a filtration system.
-It's not sexy.


00:55:09.888 --> 00:55:11.265
You could drink that water.


00:55:11.723 --> 00:55:14.935
Just send everybody home, okay?
It's time to...


00:55:15.060 --> 00:55:16.770
-If you say so.
-Okay.


00:55:16.895 --> 00:55:19.064
I'll take this, you take that.


00:55:20.440 --> 00:55:22.067
Pepper Potts.


00:55:23.402 --> 00:55:24.903
She's right. The party's over.


00:55:24.987 --> 00:55:27.948
Then again, the party was over for me,
like, an hour and a half ago.


00:55:28.073 --> 00:55:31.577
The after-party starts in 15 minutes.


00:55:35.122 --> 00:55:39.293
And if anybody, Pepper,
doesn't like it, there's the door.


00:55:45.757 --> 00:55:47.134
Yeah!


00:55:51.513 --> 00:55:52.764
Hit!


00:55:59.938 --> 00:56:11.617
Pull!


00:56:20.626 --> 00:56:22.794
I think she wants the Gallagher!


00:56:32.137 --> 00:56:34.056
I'm only gonna say this once.


00:56:37.559 --> 00:56:38.894
Get out.


00:56:45.400 --> 00:56:48.487
You don't deserve to wear one of these.
Shut it down!


00:56:50.113 --> 00:56:51.281
Goldstein.


00:56:52.533 --> 00:56:53.742
Yes, Mr Stark?


00:56:53.826 --> 00:56:57.079
Give me a phat beat
to beat my buddy's ass to.


00:57:00.874 --> 00:57:02.876
I told you to shut it down.


00:57:13.387 --> 00:57:16.974
Now, put that thing back where
you found it before someone gets hurt.


00:57:23.689 --> 00:57:24.940
Really?


00:57:32.739 --> 00:57:36.326
Sorry, pal,
but Iron Man doesn't have a sidekick.


00:57:36.910 --> 00:57:39.163
Sidekick this!


00:57:47.671 --> 00:57:49.173
Had enough?


00:57:50.090 --> 00:57:51.550
-Natalie!
-Miss Potts.


00:57:51.633 --> 00:57:53.760
Don't you "Miss Potts" me! I'm on to you.


00:57:53.844 --> 00:57:55.888
You know what?
Ever since you came here...


00:57:59.600 --> 00:58:00.642
Pepper!


00:58:02.186 --> 00:58:03.520
Get out of here. Get out of here.


00:58:09.776 --> 00:58:12.529
You want it? Take it!


00:58:53.779 --> 00:58:54.988
Put your hand down.


00:58:55.072 --> 00:58:57.282
You think you got what it takes
to wear that suit?


00:58:57.366 --> 00:58:58.659
We don't have to do this, Tony.


00:58:58.951 --> 00:59:00.619
You wanna be the War Machine,
take your shot.


00:59:00.702 --> 00:59:02.538
-Put it down!
-You gonna take a shot?


00:59:02.621 --> 00:59:03.872
-Put it down!
-No!


00:59:03.956 --> 00:59:05.415
-Drop it, Tony!
-Take it.


01:00:16.445 --> 01:00:18.864
Edwards Tower, this is Lieutenant
Colonel James Rhodes,


01:00:18.947 --> 01:00:22.159
inbound from three miles east
at 5,000 feet...

